After a previous game where my pet was polymorphed into an iron golem, I
got the impression that this was the absolute best pet to have.  He
never ate any corpses, and could kill anything with about 2 hits (the
first hit would paralyze the monster).  As a matter of fact, I was
considering polymorphing myself into an iron golem to see how tough I
would be against minotaurs, dragons and such.

But they do have a minor weakness:

"The black pudding bites spot.  Spot falls apart!"
"You see here:  an iron chain, an iron chain, an iron chain..."

Iron golems are so rare as opponents that I doubt I'll ever get the
chance to see if I could exploit that weakness in battle (maybe throw a
potion of water?).  If you polymorph into one, is there a way to protect
against being killed with one hit?

